# What NOT to upload when running `gcloud builds submit`.
#
# Without this, the build uploads the entire folder -- including the git
# history and any local Python virtual environment. That's slow, and on a
# metered connection it's wasteful. The Dockerfile copies core/app,
# core/static, core/requirements.txt and db/migrations.
#
# Note gcloud falls back to reading .gitignore when this file is absent,
# which mostly works -- but .git itself isn't in .gitignore, and it's
# usually the biggest thing in the folder.
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.env
docs/
workers/
# The schema is NOT excluded. The container applies its own migrations at
# startup, so it has to contain them -- and excluding db/ here made every
# Docker build fail on `COPY db/migrations` with no source, which on Render
# means the previous container keeps serving and the new code never lands.
# That is a silent failure: the site stays up and stays wrong.
db/*
!db/migrations/
core/tests/
